          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Is Zofdim a good treadmill brand?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              We could not tell. On 5 November 2026 we found no Zofdim website, no independent review and no retailer listing we could read, so there is no evidence either way beyond the listings themselves. Judge a Zofdim listing on its seller, return window, warranty and consistency, not the name.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Who makes Zofdim treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              We could not establish that. Many marketplace walking-pad brands are labels used by sellers for machines built by a small number of factories, but without a listing or a manual we cannot say which factory or company is behind Zofdim. The seller named on the listing is who handles returns.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Where are Zofdim treadmills sold?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Most likely on a marketplace such as Amazon, given how many people search for the name. Amazon and Walmart pages returned errors or bot checks when we tried to read them on 5 November 2026, so we could not confirm a listing. We found no other retailer carrying the name.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Has there been a Zofdim treadmill recall?</h3></summary>
